tabolite that inhibits Candida  albicans  so what he did was take his strain of  Interest  inoculate the FF microplate and incubate  it then he read it on a standard Plate  Reader to see which carbon sources in  that plate supported growth of his  organism  for those substrates that supported  growth he then scaled up into one liter  Shake flasks and measured the target  metabolite  he also took the supernatants from the  FF microplate and then used those to  test against a lawn of candida albicans  to see if there was antimicrobial  activity in the supernatant  what he found was that Genta bios and  diffractos supported the highest levels  of growth  but on his scatter plot where he was  measuring the compound of interest and  the shake flasks with the substrates  that were best for growth the highest  result was obtained with sucrose and L  ramnose not fructose or Genta bios  and when he tested those supernatants  from the FF microplate for antimicrobial  activity with candida albicans sucrose  and ramnose were the substrates that led  to the highest inhibition so we can see  from these experiments that the  preferred carbon Source can be decoupled  from the carbon source that will allow  for the highest yield or tighter of our  product of Interest  so I've shown you how the technology can  be used for all types of microbial cells  for clone selection characterization and  determining optimal growth conditions I  also want to mention that we have the  same technology optimized for mammalian  cells as well so it's same basic  technology but the compounds and  protocols were optimized for  interrogating mammalian cell lines  I've covered a couple of use cases on  strain development and characterization  as well as optimization of culture  conditions leading to higher yields but  we've also seen our technology used in  novel ways for a lot of other  applications  so I've placed a link to a publication  database on this slide so I would  encourage you to go to this li